  ├────────────────────┼──────┼──────┼──────┼──────┤
  │ B \makebox+\hfill  │ FAIL │ FAIL │ FAIL │ PASS │
  ├────────────────────┼──────┼──────┼──────┼──────┤
  │ C tabular* control │ FAIL │ FAIL │ FAIL │ PASS │
  └────────────────────┴──────┴──────┴──────┴──────┘

  B and C produce byte-identical raw extractions (diff clean). Both split each role into three blocks, and both emit
  Mar 2021 - Present after the last role's bullets. The spec's stated cause is wrong: tabular* is not the culprit. B
  removes tabular*, keeps the horizontal split, and fails identically. Horizontal separation is the cause.

  Macro to adopt, replacing template-rails-original.tex:44-50:
  
  % #1 Company  #2 Dates  #3 Title  #4 Location 
  % One source line. Everything a parser needs for one role lands on one line,
  % in one text run, in reading order. Bake-off: reports/macro-bakeoff.md
  \newcommand{\resumeSubheading}[4]{
  \vspace{-1pt}\item
    \textbf{#1} \textbar{} #3 \textbar{} #2 \textbar{} #4
    \vspace{-7pt}
  }
  
  Argument order unchanged, so no call site needs editing. \textbar{} extracts as ASCII |. An em dash would put
  U+2014 in the text layer; an ASCII hyphen would collide with the date separator Gate 0.6 looks for. Keep the field
  order Company, Title, Dates, Location: a long header wraps only after the date, so a wrap can never separate the
  date from the title (stress-tested).

  Two blockers found while building, for the Resume Architect: 
  
  1. \input{glyphtounicode} and \pdfgentounicode=1 are pdfTeX primitives. Tectonic runs XeTeX and dies on them. Guard
     with \ifdefined\pdfgentounicode ... \fi.
  2. CV-SPEC item 1's \DisableLigatures aborts the tectonic build (microtype: pdftex-only). It is also unnecessary. A
     control probe with the template's roboto font and no fix extracts efficient workflow office profile conflict 
     flag as plain ASCII, zero U+FB01. Recorded as an open question for you in the report, along with two others. I
     did not change the spec.

